diff --git a/proto/decentraland/sdk/components/avatar_shape.proto b/proto/decentraland/sdk/components/avatar_shape.proto
--- a/proto/decentraland/sdk/components/avatar_shape.proto
+++ b/proto/decentraland/sdk/components/avatar_shape.proto
@@ -13,6 +13,13 @@
 //
 // Note that, while AvatarShape can be attached to any Entity, it's only actually used in the global 
 // Avatar Scene. Other requirements are usually better served by GLTFs.
+//
+// Movement: when the scene moves an AvatarShape entity (Transform or Tween) each explorer derives the
+// locomotion animation from the motion. `keep_emote_on_move` lets a full-body emote started with
+// `expression_trigger_id` play through that motion instead. It is scene-local (never relayed to other
+// players), read only on scene-owned AvatarShape entities, and ignored on `engine.PlayerEntity` and on
+// other players' entities, whose emotes follow the explorer's own input rules. Explorers without
+// support keep their current behaviour.
 message PBAvatarShape {
   string id = 1;                  // the user ID
   optional string name = 2;       // visible name (default: "NPC")
@@ -40,5 +47,11 @@
   repeated string emotes = 11; // available emotes (default empty)
 
   optional bool show_only_wearables = 12; // hides the skin + hair + facial features (default: false)
+
+  // 13 is force_render on experimental-bevy
+  // true: a full-body emote keeps playing while the scene moves this entity (Transform or Tween); no walk/run
+  // is blended in until the emote ends or is replaced, then the explorer's locomotion rule applies again.
+  // false: today's behaviour, the explorer's locomotion rule may interrupt the emote
+  optional bool keep_emote_on_move = 14; // keep the running emote while the scene moves this entity (default: false)
 }
 
